  "notes": "{殴|なぐ}る is a transitive verb meaning to punch or strike with the fist.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Pattern: [person]を{殴|なぐ}る or [body part]を{殴|なぐ}る\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {顔|かお}を{殴|なぐ}る: to punch in the face\n- {頭|あたま}を{殴|なぐ}る: to hit on the head\n- {殴|なぐ}られる: to be punched (passive)\n- {殴|なぐ}り{合|あ}う: to fight, exchange blows\n\nRELATED 'HITTING' VERBS:\n- {殴|なぐ}る: to punch (fist, strong)\n- {叩|たた}く: to hit, slap (open hand, lighter)\n- {打|う}つ: to hit, strike (general, also for typing)\n- {蹴|け}る: to kick\n- {殴|なぐ}りつける: to strike hard, punch violently\n\nLEGAL/FORMAL TERMS:\n- {暴行|ぼうこう}: assault\n- {暴力|ぼうりょく}: violence\n- {傷害|しょうがい}: bodily injury",
